1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,299
Your portfolio should not make you piece together a dozen disconnected tools.

2
00:00:05,299 --> 00:00:13,177
Portfolio Tracker brings the day-to-day picture and the deeper research into one connected desktop workspace.

3
00:00:13,177 --> 00:00:14,739
Start with the dashboard.

4
00:00:14,739 --> 00:00:23,098
The private account total is blurred in this tour, while performance, income, risk, and portfolio health stay easy to scan.

5
00:00:23,098 --> 00:00:29,726
The Action Center then turns those signals into a practical list of items that may deserve attention.

6
00:00:29,726 --> 00:00:33,072
Move from the whole account to the holdings behind it.

7
00:00:33,072 --> 00:00:41,679
Review positions, lots, gains and losses, categories, targets, and the full story for an individual security.

8
00:00:41,679 --> 00:00:52,213
Income tools organize dividends by day, week, and month, with calendars, history, reinvestment analysis, and retirement cash-flow planning.

9
00:00:52,213 --> 00:00:58,723
When it is time to research, bring a stock, ETF, or closed-end fund into focus.

10
00:00:58,723 --> 00:01:11,471
Compare securities on the same timeline, examine distributions and NAV behavior, run valuation and technical screens, and use purpose-built buying checklists to keep the process consistent.

11
00:01:11,471 --> 00:01:24,986
Portfolio analytics adds another layer of context: allocation, diversification, sector exposure, correlations, risk and return, consolidation opportunities, and the current macro environment.

12
00:01:24,986 --> 00:01:33,216
Planning tools can model portfolios, test alternatives, set targets, and preview a rebalance before any decision is made.

13
00:01:33,216 --> 00:01:36,588
Options workflows live in the same application.

14
00:01:36,588 --> 00:01:51,966
Track open and closed trades, estimate probabilities, explore payoff and risk graphs, learn each strategy, and scan for setups across covered calls, cash-secured puts, spreads, condors, butterflies, and more.

15
00:01:51,966 --> 00:01:59,205
Tax tools bring annual reporting, gains and losses, blended yield, and tax-loss harvesting into view.

16
00:01:59,205 --> 00:02:07,265
Import and export workflows help keep the data portable, while Split View lets you compare two screens or accounts side by side.

17
00:02:07,265 --> 00:02:09,882
Finally, make the workspace your own.

18
00:02:09,882 --> 00:02:18,229
Reorder or hide navigation, choose a focused role preset, adjust settings, and open detailed help whenever you need it.

19
00:02:18,229 --> 00:02:23,424
One place to monitor, research, compare, plan, and learn.

20
00:02:23,424 --> 00:02:25,052
Portfolio Tracker.

21
00:02:25,052 --> 00:02:29,401
See the whole portfolio, and understand what is driving it.

